# ==== T-FMT-D (R41) fill-pack matrix — LIST KIND = GENERIC-PARAMETER list.
#
# SUBJECT: this fixture asserts `gg fmt` OUTPUT (byte-for-byte, in
# `fmt_fill_pack_generic_params_kind`) — a bulk `gg fmt` sweep MUST EXCLUDE it.
#
# Emit site: `Formatter::format_generic_params_wrapped` -> the delimited-list
# chokepoint `emit_delimited_list("[", "]", ..)` -> `doc::surround_fill`.
#
# Axis cell claim (Core #12 — `list kind x fit` for the GENERIC-PARAM kind ONLY):
#   GpFlat  fits-flat          one line, no trailing comma
#   GpFill  needs-fill         greedy packing at the block continuation indent
#   GpOver  single-over-width  the one type parameter does not fit on the open line,
#                              so it breaks to the continuation indent, alone
#
# The EMPTY cell has no spelling here: `struct S[]:` is a parse error, so the
# generic-param list is only ever absent, never empty. (`p_empty` in `params.gg`
# and `c_empty` in `call_args.gg` cover the empty branch of the packer.)
#
# RED source per row: GpFill / GpOver are TRUE pre-fix REDs (one type parameter
# per line with a trailing comma). GpFlat is invariant — break-and-restore it by
# lowering `doc::MAX_WIDTH`.
struct GpFlat[Aaaa, Bbbb, Cccc]:
    int x

struct GpFill[Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa, Bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb, Cccccccccccccccc, Dddddddddddddddd, Eeeeeeeeeeeeeeee, Ffffffffffffffff, Gggggggggggggggg]:
    int x

struct GpOver[ASingleTypeParameterNameWhoseRenderedWidthAloneExceedsTheEntireLineWidthBudgetOfTheGorgetFormatterEvenAtIndent]:
    int x
